me>FUJIMOTO, HISAYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KISHIMOTO, TOKIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ONISHI, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An image reader (A) includes a plurality of light sources (6) arranged in line, the light from which travels through a channel (14) and irradiates a linear read area (S). The channel (14) is divided into a plurality of sections (14a) by a plurality of partitions (15). Thus, uniform brightness is obtained in the whole part of the linear read area (S), including both ends and the central part.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un lecteur (A) d'image comprenant une pluralité de sources (6) lumineuses disposées en ligne. La lumière émise par ces sources passe à travers un canal (14) et illumine une zone (S) de lecture linéaire. Le canal (14) est divisé en une pluralité de sections (14a) par une pluralité d'éléments (15) séparateurs. Une luminosité uniforme est ainsi obtenue sur la totalité de la zone (S) de lecture, y compris les deux extrémités et la partie centrale.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>